==Rules==
{{ColosseumRule|Plus One: Uber}}

==Battleground==
*The enemy base is protected by a [[Base Barrier]] until the boss is defeated.
*Infinite [[Snache]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Gabriel]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.
*7 [[Angelic Gory|Angelic Gories]] spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 40~46.67 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,400f</sup>.
*1 [[Cala Maria]] spawns after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>.
*2 [[Lutrinae Gokurakko]]s spawn after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>, delay 66.67~73.33 seconds<sup>2,000f~2,200f</sup>.
*1 [[Pterowl Hazuku]] spawns as the boss after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>.
*1 [[Winged Pigge]] spawns after 90 seconds<sup>2,700f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage is hell. From the two Gokurakkos, to the Cala Maria that snipes any of your Ubers, to Winged Pigge making killing anything a hassle, to the Hazuku in the back that snipes your anti-Angel counters, this is by far the hardest stage in the entirety of the Otherworld Colosseum. Whereas the other four stages were very pressurizing, but still doable to an extent without Ubers, this one is almost straight up impossible without them. Do not even try to do this stage without Ubers unless you enjoy suffering.

There are two main ways to play this stage: either rush Hazuku, or suffer through everyone here. Irregardless of what strategy you choose, kill Cala Maria as fast as possible, and bring a Rich Cat to afford the Ubers that you're going to need to send out.

If you choose to rush Hazuku down, you'll need to do it fast before Winged Pigge spawns, which gives you 30 seconds to win. Units like [[Fishman Cat]], Talented [[Awakened Bahamut Cat]], [[Master of Mind Soractes (Special Cat)|Soractes]] and melee Ubers do the trick. In a pinch, remember that Uber Summons are doubled under this condition, which can give you a quick and easy 160k damage if needed.

If you choose to tank everyone here, you're going to need very strong Ubers. See the Recommended Ubers section for more information.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Food Stall Cat (Rare Cat)|Cafeteria Cat]]: Cafeteria Cat uses many abilities that are very good in this stage. His [[Massive Damage]] against [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel Enemies]] allows him to quickly take on Gabriel, Cala Maria and Gokurakko. His [[Curse]] ability prevents Gokurakko from pushing further in your defense and disables Winged Pigge's powerful [[Weaken]]. Unfortunately, he doesn't have enough health to survive Winged Pigge's attacks without being knocked back and he has [[Single Attack|Single Target]] where he could hit an unwanted target.
*[[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]]: Courier Cat's high speed and low range would be quite essential to infiltrate Hazuku's blind spot and deal huge damage to it with Courier Cat's [[Behemoth Slayer]]. It can also help to kill any oncoming peons for Cafeteria Cat as long as Courier has not been weakened.
*[[Bubble Cat]]: Bubble is an extremely strong unit. While he has very little HP, his effective damage is ridiculously high and he has Weaken Immune for Winged Pigge.
*[[Reunion Li'l Rei]]: Rei is a very strong unit here, given her decent mobility, her ability to Weaken the ferocious frontline, her being Immune to Weaken, as well as her decently good base health for tanking Hazuku.
*[[Master of Mind Soractes (Special Cat)|Master of Mind Soractes]]: Soractes's fast attacks, high piercing range and decent [[Freeze]] chances allows him to consistantly freeze Winged Pigge and other Angel peons to prevent them from being to close to your frontlines. Additionally, his high speed and low range will be useful for getting inside Hazuku's blind spot.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
Due to this Colosseum's Rule, any Uber Rare Cats mentioned will be twice as effective.

*Rushers: Examples include [[E. Honda (Uber Rare Cat)|E.Honda]] and [[Oni Battlepod Kozuchimaru]]. These units' mobility gives them a strong advantage, allowing them to rush in, get a huge amount of damage in, and be avaliable for another round quickly.
*Tankers: Examples include [[Tekachi (Uber Rare Cat)|Tetsukachi]], [[King Gamereon]] and [[Holiday Juvens CC]]. These units need to be boosted to do anything here given the skyrocketting DPS here.
*Nukers: Examples include [[Jizo's Mega-Castle]], [[Dynasaurus Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Dynasaurus Cat]] and [[Obliterator Diabolosa]]. While these units are extremely weak to Hazuku's hits, combined with the Slow Beam or Thunderbolt cannon, they can deliver huge damage to the frontline and allow you to clean the stage up quicker. Notably, Jizo has a first form that can deliver huge damage against the Gokurakko, Dynasaurus has a Summon and Diabolosa has a Damage Up combo that make them worth running irregardless.
*[[Thunder Jack (Uber Rare Cat)|Thunder Jack]]: Thunder Jack's Normal Form is a powerful unit in this stage. Despite the peons in this stage and his single target, if he is paired with good [[:Category:Area Attack Cats|Area Attackers]], he can potentially stunlock the Winged Pigge out of your cats' range with his [[Knockback]] and allow you to deal immensive damage against Hazuku. If he does get hit by Winged Pigge, don't worry as he is [[Immune to Weaken]]. Make sure to support him well against the Gokurakkos as their DPS can easily kill Thunder Jack and leave you helpless.
*[[The Grateful Crane (Uber Rare Cat)|Supernova Cosmo]]: Supernova Cosmo is extremely fragile, but if he lands a hit, it will be devastating, freezing everything on the field for 5 seconds alongside dealing his huge damage. He can't land direct hits on Hazuku due to being outranged, so waiting until Winged Pigge or other enemies are on the field to use as stepping stones is necessary.
*[[Squirtgun Saki (Uber Rare Cat)|Aquablaster Saki]]: Aquablaster Saki is similar to Supernova Cosmo, except she trades crowd-control and range for damage and survivability. At Lv.50, she'll have 182,250 health and 194,400 damage against all the enemies in this stage, and it's easier for her to land hits in comparison to Cosmo due to her shorter foreswing. The enemies can rush into her blind spot though, so using Ramen Cat and Stone Cat with her is highly recommended.

